// PIN GLB-003 — one unused variable per SITE, not per name.
//
// Two loops, two iterators, neither used. The Rust engines kept declarations in
// a map keyed by NAME, so the second `i` displaced the first and one warning
// came out — pointing at one of the two sites and silently dropping the other.
// The browser engine warned twice all along.
//
// A warning carries a position, so one warning for two sites is not a shorter
// report: it is a report about one of them. Decided and closed 2026-08-30.
@ i:1..3 { s = °s "x" }
@ i:1..3 { t = °t "y" }
>> s t ¶

// Y la mitad que no debe cambiar: un nombre prefijado con `_` sigue sin avisar,
// las veces que haga falta.
@ _k:1..2 { u = °u "z" }
@ _k:1..2 { v = °v "w" }
>> u v ¶
